      "content": "The Algerian War of Independence (1954-1962) was a pivotal struggle against French colonial rule. The National Liberation Front (FLN) launched a series of attacks on August 1, 1954, igniting a fierce resistance. Key events include the Battle of Algiers (1956-1957), where FLN guerrillas waged a brutal urban warfare against French forces, and the Evian Accords (1962), which finally led to Algerian independence. Throughout the war, the Algerian people endured immense suffering, but their relentless fight for freedom ultimately triumphed, ending over 130 years of French colonial domination. The FLN's guerrilla tactics, political savvy, and the unwavering support of the Algerian populace were crucial in their eventual victory.",
